*******************************************************************************************                                                                                        **		Apple IIgs Printer Driver                                                        **                                                                                        **		File: metrics.a -- Exclusive print record access and dimension calculations      **                                                                                        **		Written by Ben Koning                                                            **		Copyright (C) 1991 Apple Computer, Inc.                                          **                                                                                        *******************************************************************************************							include		'equates.h'							include		'm16.util'							include		'e16.print'							include		'm16.intmath'							include		'e16.quickdraw'							include		'm16.quickdraw'MetricsProc					proc		export**METRICS (PAGE MEASUREMENT) MODEL AND IMPLEMENTATION:**All information related to page size, print quality, etc., options is stored in a data*structure called the Print Record, the memory for which is the application's responsibility*(a print record should be maintained with each document enacted on by an application so that*page setup information stays with a letter, drawing, etc.), and the contents of which are*the responsibility of the currently selected printer driver.**The routines in this module seek to isolate the rest of this printer driver from the specifics*of the contents of the user's print record.  They also arbitrate between the realms of page*measurements in inches and rectangle sizes in pixels.**There are a set of GetXXX and SetXXX routines below, which must be called rather than*modifying the print record directly.  Before a SetXXX completes, it causes a calculation*routine to be called which ensures that the print record stays self-consistent.**The calculation routine uses the paper type and selected sizing options to find values for*several rectangles, used by applications as well as the rest of this driver, and stores them.**From the paper type, its paper dimensions are looked up from a table.  This information is*stored in the rPaper rectangle.  Thus dimensions could be different for Letter, Legal,*Envelope, etc.  The vertical dimension is used, for example, to set the page length so that*form feed works correctly.  rPaper is given in pixels.**Margins are subtracted from the rPaper rectangle to create the rPage rectangle, the actual*printable area inside a sheet of paper.  The first point of rPage is made the origin, so*that the first point of rPaper is negative.  rPage is given in pixels.**Note that the sizing settings (Vertical Condense, Reduction, Page Gap) actually increase the*effective printing area.  They are not just effects settings which would affect only the*outcome of the printing.  In other words, selecting 50%-size means that the application can*give the user more drawing space, for example.  Also, Landscape means that the paper is still*inserted normally into the printer; just that the X & Y dimensions that the application sees*are reversed.  In other words, selecting Landscape means that a drawing application's rulers*show 11" left to right and 8" top to bottom for 8x11" paper.**The metrics calculations usually proceed as follows:**		Get resolution in pixels/inch from equates based on port/land orientation setting* 		If vertical condense, double y resolution* 		If reduction, multiply x,y resolutions accordingly* 		If 320 mode, half x resolution* 		Divide x,y resolutions by 2 to convert from Imaging resolution to rPage res (see below)* 		Get paper_x, paper_y, paper_gap size in inches from table based on paper type setting* 		Multiply dimensions by resolutions to convert dimensions to pixels* 		rPaper gets physical page dimensions with rPage first point as origin* 		rPage gets page dimensions minus a border based horizontally on equates and vertically* 			on the paper_gap and the page gap setting* 		Landscape orientation causes rPaper and rPage to have x & y exchanged**For this particular printer driver, reduction and landscape modes are not supported.**In addition to providing the application with information about the printable area, the rPage*rectangle is used as the source rectangle during picture recording (QDAux's OpenPicture,*ClosePicture, DrawPicture, etc).  When DrawPicture is called, the playback rectangle may be*the same size or may be bigger to allow for higher quality printing (the GetImagingSize routine*returns the playback size based on rPage and the quality setting).**Two pixel-level units are defined for internal use: "rPage" units and "Imaging" units.  RPage*dimensions change with respect to the option settings which increase printable area real estate,*as described above, but remain constant with respect to the Standard or Better quality mode*setting.  Imaging units, on the other hand, are equal to rPage units with a scaling factor*applied to facilitate higher resolution when printing at denser dot pitches.  For example, if*rPage.X2 is "100" and the quality is "standard", then ImagingSize.X2 would be "100".  But if*rPage.X2 is "100" and the quality is "better", then ImagingSize.X2 could be "200".  Several*"ConvertRPageToImgSize" routines are provided as the exclusive converters between these two units.*Thus, in summary: rPage is the amount of pixels that the application sees for the positioning*of QD objects, while the Imaging size is the amount of pixels that the driver has to deal with*when playing back the picture containing these objects, thus obtaining high resolution on the*printed paper since there "are more dots" in QD objects, causing smoother contours.***STARTPRH: Call to use print record from handle; sets up ParamLongA with pointer:*StartPRH					ldy			#4						;lock handle							lda			[printRecordHandle],y							ora			#$8000							sta			[printRecordHandle],y							lda			[printRecordHandle]		;deref to get ptr in ParamLongA							sta			ParamLongA+0							ldy			#2							lda			[printRecordHandle],y							sta			ParamLongA+2							rts**FINISHPRH: Call this when done working with print record handle:*FinishPRH					ldy			#4							lda			[printRecordHandle],y							and			#$7FFF							sta			[printRecordHandle],y							rts			**INITPRINTRECORD: Fills user's print record with default values, for both ex- and internal use.*On entry, printRecordHandle must be set.*							export		InitPrintRecordInitPrintRecord											jsr			SetMiscAdv				;setup miscellaneous and advanced*							lda			#paperTypeUsaLetter		;standard paper size							sta			OptionA							jsr			SetPaper*							lda			#1						;high print quality							sta			OptionA							jsr			SetQuality*							stz			OptionA					;normal (tall) vertical size							jsr			SetVSize*							lda			#1						;print all pages							sta			OptionA							lda			#32767							sta			OptionB							jsr			SetPageRange*							lda			#1						;automatic sheet feed							sta			OptionA							jsr			SetFeed*							lda			#1						;one copy							sta			OptionA							brl			SetCopies							**OPTION SETTING ROUTINES: These modify the user's print record in DP variable "printRecord". They*are called as a result of default, validate, style, or job calls.  They leave the print record in*an uncorrupted state.  Unlike the old driver, we rely only on the offsets provided in the include*file, for future portability.  The parameter to be set is passed in the DP variables "OptionA" and*"OptionB".  For boolean values (such as portrait/landscape, etc), 0 means the default option:**NOTE: These routines should be the only entities within this driver to modify the print record.*An internal coding, which makes sense by using 0 for default values, etc., is used to refer to*values of print record settings, and backward compatiblity may demand that certain values be stored*in a reverse or bizarre sense in the print record.  It is the purpose of these Get/Set routines*to perform any such translation.**SETMISCADV: Initializes miscellaneous and advanced option switches and normally-nil fields:							export		SetMiscAdvSetMiscAdv							jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprVersion					;Version ID							lda			#VersionID							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#oprInfo+oiDev				;Device ID							lda			#DeviceID					;(1=IW 2=LQ 3=LW 4=Epson etc)							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							lda			#0							;0,0 first coords of rPage							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh1							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov1							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;set wDev to 0's + defaults							lda			#wDevGap+wDevReduction+wDevVSize+wDevOrientation							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							shortm							ldy			#oprJob+obJDocLoop							lda			#$00						;Set byte for immediate method							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#oprJob+ofFromUser							lda			#$01						;Set the from-user field byte							sta			[ParamLongA],y							longm*							ldy			#owResScaling				;Setup the blow-up amount value							lda			#5							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							lda			#0*							ldy			#oprJob+opIdleProc							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;Default NIL idleproc							iny							iny							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETQUALITY: Sets print loop method and imaging size determinant (0/1==180/360dpi):							export		SetQualitySetQuality					jsr			StartPRH							lda			OptionA							ldy			#owQuality			;put code in new quality word							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprStl+owDev		;now ensure wDev Better bit set right							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#ÅwDevBetter							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			OptionA							cpx			#1							bne			SeQuSetBJD							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ora			#wDevBetter							sta			[ParamLongA],ySeQuSetBJD					lda			#$00				;ensure bJDocLoop set to 0 because this							ldy			#oprJob+obJDocLoop	;printer driver works in immediate-mode							shortm							sta			[ParamLongA],y							longm							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETPAPER: Sets the paper type, used for calculating printable area dimensions:							export		SetPaperSetPaper					jsr 		StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+opaperType							lda			OptionA							sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETVSIZE: Sets vertical sizing, normal or 50% ("condensed") for correct font aspect ratio:							export		SetVSizeSetVSize					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			OptionA							bne			@ClearIt					;reverse sense!							ora			#wDevVSize							bra			@StoreIt@ClearIt					and			#ÅwDevVSize@StoreIt					sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETFEED: Sets automatic/manual page feed if passed 1/0:							export		SetFeedSetFeed						jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+ofeed							lda			OptionA							sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETPAGERANGE: Sets range of pages to be processed (others are ignored and not recorded):														export		SetPageRange				;OptionA/B = first/last 1..xSetPageRange				jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+oiFstPage							lda			OptionA							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprJob+oiLstPage							lda			OptionB							sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETCOPIES: Sets number of copies to produce for each page:														export		SetCopies					;OptionA = # copies 1..xSetCopies					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+oiCopies							lda			OptionA							sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*Common exit sequence:							CalcAndFinishPRH			jsr			CalcMetrics							brl			FinishPRH**INFORMATION INQUIRY ROUTINES: These routines return (possibly processed) info about pr rec items:*NOTE: These routines return data in EITHER accumulator OR zero flag status OR X/Y registers.*NOTE: These routines return 0 for the common default settings; may be inverse of wDev.**GETOKOURDRIVER: Sets zero flag (BEQ test) if DeviceID AND VersionID came from our driver:							export		GetOkOurDriverGetOkOurDriver				jsr			StartPRH					;get and lock handle							ldy			#oprInfo+oiDev				;DeviceID offset							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;get it							cmp			#DeviceID					;zero flag set/clr if yes/no ours							bne			InqExitZFlag				;nope, was different printer							ldy			#oprVersion					;VersionID offset							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;get it							cmp			#VersionID					;zero flag set/clr if yes/no oursInqExitZFlag				php										;zero flag set on exit							jsr			FinishPRH					;unlock handle							plp										;zero flag valid again							rts										;exit							*GETPAPER: Returns the paper type in A:							export		GetPaperGetPaper					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+opaperType							lda			[ParamLongA],yInqExitACC					pha							jsr			FinishPRH							pla							rts							*GETQUALITY: Gets quality mode in A (0=180dpi, 1=360dpi):							export		GetQualityGetQuality					jsr			StartPRH					;lock and dereference							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;look at wDev.Better bit							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevBetter							bne			GeQuForceTo1				;if wDev.Better=1 -> set to 1GeQuForceTo0				lda			#0							;here if wDev.Better=0							ldy			#owQuality					;if wDev.Better=0 -> set to 0							sta			[ParamLongA],y							bra			GeQuGetQualityGeQuForceTo1				lda			#1							ldy			#owQuality							sta			[ParamLongA],yGeQuGetQuality				ldy			#owQuality					;now get info from new place							lda			[ParamLongA],y							brl			InqExitACC					;unlock and exit with ACC set							*GETVSIZE: Gets vertical sizing normal/condensed, 0/1 respectively, in A:							export		GetVSizeGetVSize					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevVSize							eor			#wDevVSize					;reverse sense of wDev bit!							beq			GetVSizeDone							lda			#1GetVSizeDone				brl			InqExitACC							*GETFEED: Gets manual page feed option in zero flag (BEQ if manual page feed):							export		GetFeedGetFeed						jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+oFeed							lda			[ParamLongA],y							brl			InqExitZFlag							*GETPAGERANGE: Gets page range (First Page -> X; Last Page -> Y):							export		GetPageRangeGetPageRange				jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+oiFstPage							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							ldy			#oprJob+oiLstPage							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							jsr			FinishPRH							ply							plx							rts*GETCOPIES: Gets number of copies to be printed in A:							export		GetCopiesGetCopies					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+oiCopies							lda			[ParamLongA],y							brl			InqExitACC							*GETIDLEPROC: Gets optional user-select IdleProc called during imaging (lo->X, hi->Y, carry):							export		GetIdleProcGetIdleProc					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+opIdleProcInqExitWithYpXYPtrData		lda			[ParamLongA],y				;exit with pointer given in							pha										;print record field at offset							iny										;in y in lo->x, hi->y, and							iny										;set carry if non-nil...							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							jsr			FinishPRH							ply							plx							stx			ParamLongA							tya							ora			ParamLongA							cmp			#1							rts							*GETRPAGESIZE: Gets bottom right coordinates of last calculated rPage field in pixels (->X,Y):							export		GetRPageSizeGetRPageSize				jsr			StartPRH					;access print record fields							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							jsr			FinishPRH							ply										;return Y size in Y							plx										;return X size in X							rts*GETIMAGINGSIZE: Gets bottom right coordinates of how big the offscrn pix buff should be (->X,Y):							export		GetImagingSizeGetImagingSize				jsr			StartPRH					;lock print rec struct & deref							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2			;access X page size in scrn pix							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;convert to pr pix and push							jsr			ConvertRPageToImgSizeX							pha							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2			;access Y page size in scrn pix							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;convert to pr pix and push							jsr			ConvertRPageToImgSizeY							pha							jsr			FinishPRH					;release print record							ply										;return magnified Y size in Y							plx										;return magnified X size in X							rts*GETMODEBYTE: Gets 320/640 mode byte at the time of print record formation in A:							export		GetModeByteGetModeByte					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+ointernA							lda			[ParamLongA],y							brl			InqExitACC*GETISFEATUREERROR: Returns 0 if ok, 1 if unsupported features set in print record, in A:							export		GetIsFeatureErrorGetIsFeatureError			jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;get wDev bits							and			#wDevUSFmask				;mask out the ones not supported							cmp			#wDevUSFshould				;check w/ our settings for these							beq			GeFeIsGoodGeFeIsBad					lda			#1							brl			InqExitACCGeFeIsGood					lda			#0							brl			InqExitACC*GETLINELAYOUTDISABLE: Gets if line layout is enabled/disabled, 0/1 respectively, in A:							export		GetLineLayoutDisableGetLineLayoutDisable		jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevNoLineLayout							beq			GeLdDone							lda			#1GeLdDone					brl			InqExitACC*GETSTATMESGDISABLE: Gets if status message box is enabled/disabled, 0/1 respectively, in A:							export		GetStatMesgDisableGetStatMesgDisable			jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevNoStatusBox							beq			GeMdDone							lda			#1GeMdDone					brl			InqExitACC*GETFORCETXMDISABLE: Gets if forcing text mode to OR to avoid clip is enabled/disabled, 0/1, in A:							export		GetForceTxMDisableGetForceTxMDisable			jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevNoForceTextMode							beq			GeTdDone							lda			#1GeTdDone					brl			InqExitACC*GET640PIXMAPDISABLE: Gets if special 640 pixelmap handling is enabled/disabled, 0/1, in A:							export		Get640PixMapDisableGet640PixMapDisable			jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevNo640PixMap							beq			GePmDone							lda			#1GePmDone					brl			InqExitACC**METRICS UNITS CONVERSION ROUTINES: These private internal routines convert between application-*level ("rPage") and imaging-level ("Imaging") (which are possibly magnified) coordinate units.*These routines should be the exclusive converters betwen these units.  They assume that a valid*print record handle exists and that StartPRH has been called already, so that ParamLongA contains*a pointer to the temporarily-locked print record.  Input and output is passed and returned in A.***CONVERTRPAGETOIMGSIZEX: Horizontal rPage->Img [pict.source(small)->pict.dest(big)]: In/Out -> A:*ConvertRPageToImgSizeX		sta			CoRpCoordValue				;save input given in A							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;look at wDev.Better bit							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;pr rec hdl must be dereferenced							and			#wDevBetter					;now have quality setting; put							tax										;in X: 0=180dpi, nonzero=360dpi														lda			CoRpCoordValue				;save original value in A							asl			CoRpCoordValue				;now it's *2 in place							asl			CoRpCoordValue				;now it's *4 in place							asl			CoRpCoordValue				;now it's *8 in place							clc										;add orginal in A to in-place-							adc			CoRpCoordValue				;value to get *9 in A							lsr a									;/2 to get *4.5 in A							sta			CoRpCoordValue				;store to get *4.5 in place							txa										;restore quality setting in A							bne			CoRpXIts4p5x				;0=2.25x(180dpi),>0=4.5x(360dpi)CoRpXIts2p25x				lsr			CoRpCoordValue				;do /2 to get *2.25 in placeCoRpXIts4p5x							lda			CoRpCoordValue				;get result in A and exit							rts**Common static working storage for both routines:*CoRpCoordValue				dc.w		0**CONVERTRPAGETOIMGSIZEY: Vertical rPage->Img [pict.source(small)->pict.dest(big)]: In/Out -> A:*ConvertRPageToImgSizeY		sta			CoRpCoordValue				;save input given in A							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;look at wDev.Better bit							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;pr rec hdl must be dereferenced							and			#wDevBetter					;now have quality setting; put							tax										;in X: 0=180dpi, nonzero=360dpi														lda			CoRpCoordValue				;save original value in A							asl			CoRpCoordValue				;now it's *2 in place							asl			CoRpCoordValue				;now it's *4 in place							clc										;add orginal in A to in-place-							adc			CoRpCoordValue				;value to get *5 in A							sta			CoRpCoordValue				;store to get *5 in place							txa										;restore quality setting in A							bne			CoRpYIts5x					;0=2.5x(180dpi),>0=5x(360dpi)CoRpYIts2p5x				lsr			CoRpCoordValue				;do /2 to get *2.5 in placeCoRpYIts5x							lda			CoRpCoordValue				;get result in A and exit							rts**CALCMETRICS: This routine sets iH/Vres, crWidth, rPage and rPaper in print record based*on the option bit and page type settings in the print record.  This routine must be called*after any print record modification to assure self-consistency.**NOTE: This is the only routine other than the Get/Set routines which may access the print record*directly, and thus is subject to backward print record flag compatibility issues.*							export		CalcMetrics*Lock and dereference the user's print record:CalcMetrics					jsr			StartPRH					;lock/deref*Save wDev field for repeated use:							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;get & save wDev for use...							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							*Start with addressable resolution; new equates assume 1X/V.Condensed/640:							ldx			#appResPortraitX			;assume portrait orientation							ldy			#appResPortraitYnoVC		;P: default not V.Condensed							stx			ParamWordA					;pwA & pwB will build iH/VRes							sty			ParamWordB							*Double Y resolution if Vertical Condense mode is on (increases printable area):							pla										;get wDev...							pha							and			#wDevVSize							bne			CalcMetricsNotCondensed							asl			ParamWordB					;double Y resolution if VCCalcMetricsNotCondensed*1/2 X res if 320 mode.  Also, store mode bit in "internA" for future band buff alloc calc:							pha							_GetMasterSCB							pla							and			#$80							ldy			#oprStl+ointernA							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;320/640 mode -> oprStl.internA							cmp			#$80							beq			CalcMetricsNot320			;branch if 640 mode active							lsr			ParamWordA					;half X resolution if 320 modeCalcMetricsNot320*We now have effective iHres and iVres that will be produced by imager in printer-pixels per inch:							ldy			#oprInfo+oiHres							lda			ParamWordA							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprInfo+oiVres							lda			ParamWordB							sta			[ParamLongA],y*Now that we have iH&Vres, we will calculate rPage&rPaper&crWidth in inch*16 based on paper type:*Get dimensions of current paper type:							ldy			#oprStl+opaperType							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;get paper type ID							cmp			#maxPaperTypeID+1			;make sure it's in range							bcc			CalcMetricsPtOk							lda			#0							;else assume and set type 0							sta			[ParamLongA],yCalcMetricsPtOk				asl	a									;paper type * 6							asl a							clc							adc			[ParamLongA],y							clc							adc			[ParamLongA],y							tax										;index into paper dimension table							lda			CalcMetricsPtTbl+0,x		;get X dimension in 1/16th inches							sta			ParamWordC					;paper X size in ParamWordC							lda			CalcMetricsPtTbl+2,x		;get Y dimension							sta			ParamWordD					;paper Y size in ParamWordD							lda			CalcMetricsPtTbl+4,x		;get -GAP value							sta			ParamWordE					;paper -GAP size in ParamWordE*If current paper type doesn't allow use of cut-sheet feeder, force manual-feed mode:							ldy			#oprStl+opaperType							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;get paper type ID							cmp			#paperTypeEurB5				;if B5 or Envelope,							beq			CalcMetricsSetForceManFd	;force manual feed							cmp			#paperTypeEnvNo10							bne			CalcMetricsDoneForceManFdCalcMetricsSetForceManFd	ldy			#oprStl+ofeed							lda			#0							sta			[ParamLongA],yCalcMetricsDoneForceManFd*If Gap option is turned off, zero our looked-up page -1*GAP value (~GAP increases printable area):							pla										;get wDev...							pha							and			#wDevGap							bne			CalcMetricsYesGap			;branch if we DO have vert gap							stz			ParamWordE					;else, no gap: zero gap valueCalcMetricsYesGap*Set external historical version of crWidth abs right margin, not used in this driver:							lda			#prRecCrWidth				;store the constant crWidth							ldy			#oprStl+ocrWidth			;value which apps have come to							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;expect in the print record							*rPaper.X1 = 0 - printLineMargin (black mark on bail) (rPage.X1.Y1=0,0 is origin) (assuming Portrt):							lda			#((ÅprintLineMargin)+1)		;-1*printLineMargin always							ldy			#orPaper+oh1				;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y							*rPaper.X2 = rPaper.X1 + paper_size.X (rPage.X1.Y1=0,0 is origin) (assuming Portrait):							clc										;X1 still in acc							adc			ParamWordC					;add X size of paper type							ldy			#orPaper+oh2				;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y							*rPaper.Y1 = 0 - GAP (rPage.X1.Y1=0,0 is origin) (assuming Portrait):							lda			ParamWordE					;get -1*GAP for current paper							ldy			#orPaper+ov1				;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y							*rPaper.Y2 = rPaper.Y1 + paper_size.Y (rPage.X1.Y1=0,0 is origin) (assuming Portrait):							clc										;Y1 still in acc							adc			ParamWordD					;add Y size of paper type							ldy			#orPaper+ov2				;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y							*rPage.X1 and rPage.Y1 are both zero and are the origin for all other rPage/rPaper coordinates:							lda			#0							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh1							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov1							sta			[ParamLongA],y							*rPage.X2 = paper_size.X - 2*printLineMargin (black mark on bail) (assuming Portrait):							lda			ParamWordC					;get X size of paper type							sec										;subtract for left&right border							sbc			#2*printLineMargin							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2			;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y							*rPage.Y2 = paper_size.Y - 2*GAP value (assuming Portrait):							lda			ParamWordE					;get gap value (-1*GAP or 0)							clc							adc			ParamWordE					;now it's -2*GAP							clc										;add Y size of paper type; now...							adc			ParamWordD					;...we've done paperY-2*GAP							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2			;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y							*Right now, rPage/rPaper are in values of inch*16. Now convert all of these to the printing pixels*that the application sees by signed multiply by our internal iHres/iVres and signed divide by 16:							ldy			#orPaper+oh1				;get value just computed above...							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;in a-reg. This is negative!							eor			#$FFFF						;negate it...							clc										;...so the unsigned convert...							adc			#1							;...will work correctly							ldx			ParamWordA					;get resolution A)iHres B)iVres							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPaper X1							eor			#$FFFF						;negate it...							clc										;...again...							adc			#1							;...back to negative							ldy			#orPaper+oh1				;store value just converted...							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;back into print record*														ldy			#orPaper+ov1							lda			[ParamLongA],y							eor			#$FFFF						;negate -> positive							clc							adc			#1							ldx			ParamWordB							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPaper Y1							eor			#$FFFF						;negate -> negative							clc							adc			#1							ldy			#orPaper+ov1							sta			[ParamLongA],y*														ldy			#orPaper+oh2				;all others are all positive...							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			ParamWordA							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPaper X2							ldy			#orPaper+oh2							sta			[ParamLongA],y*														ldy			#orPaper+ov2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			ParamWordB							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPaper Y2							ldy			#orPaper+ov2							sta			[ParamLongA],y*														ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			ParamWordA							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPage X2							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2							sta			[ParamLongA],y*														ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			ParamWordB							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPage Y2							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2							sta			[ParamLongA],y							*Copy the PrInfo subrecord to PrInfoPT for compatibility reasons:							ldy			#oprInfo+12					;source: prInfo offset							ldx			#oprInfoPT+12				;destination: prInfoPT offsetCaMeCopyPrInfoLp			lda			[ParamLongA],y				;length: 14 bytes							phy							txy							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ply							dex							dex							dey							dey							cpy			#oprInfo							bcs			CaMeCopyPrInfoLp*Exit:							pla										;get rid of wDev on stack							brl			FinishPRH					;return via lock routine**The following subroutine does AREG := (AREG*XREG)/16 with unsigned math to cvt inches -> pixels:*CalcMetricsConvert			pha										;result space for multiply							pha										;result space for multiply							pha										;A REG: value to be converted							phx										;X REG: resolution iHres/iVres							_Multiply							pulllong	ParamLongB					;get hi and lo words							lsr			ParamLongB+2				;divide by 2 hi word							ror			ParamLongB+0				;divide by 2 lo word	=/2							lsr			ParamLongB+2				;divide by 2 hi word							ror			ParamLongB+0				;divide by 2 lo word	=/4							lsr			ParamLongB+2				;divide by 2 hi word							ror			ParamLongB+0				;divide by 2 lo word	=/8							lsr			ParamLongB+2				;divide by 2 hi word							ror			ParamLongB+0				;divide by 2 lo word	=/16							lda			ParamLongB+0				;get lo word only in ACC							rts										;we're done							**Lookup table containing physical dimensions (in inch * 16) of different types of paper:*CalcMetricsPtTbl			dc.w		paperSizeUsaLetterX			;indexed if paper type == 0							dc.w		paperSizeUsaLetterY			;type 0 must be US Letter							dc.w		-1*paperSizeUsaLetterGap							dc.w		paperSizeUsaLegalX			;indexed if paper type == 1							dc.w		paperSizeUsaLegalY			;type 1 must be US Legal							dc.w		-1*paperSizeUsaLegalGap														dc.w		paperSizeEurA4X				;indexed if paper type == 2							dc.w		paperSizeEurA4Y				;type 2 must be A4 Letter							dc.w		-1*paperSizeEurA4Gap														dc.w		paperSizeEurB5X				;indexed if paper type == 3							dc.w		paperSizeEurB5Y							dc.w		-1*paperSizeEurB5Gap														dc.w		paperSizeEnvNo10X			;indexed if paper type == 4							dc.w		paperSizeEnvNo10Y							dc.w		-1*paperSizeEnvNo10Gap							endproc							end